#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
. "$HERE/apptainer_shim/setup.sh"

CMD="${1:-}"
case "$CMD" in
    doctor) _apt_doctor; exit $? ;;
    ""|-h|--help|help)
        cat <<'USAGE'
d710_apptainer -- exactly `./d710`, with apptainer instead of docker.

  ./d710_apptainer doctor                        check this machine first
  ./d710_apptainer exam --raw D --ct D --case N  everything else: ./d710 --help

A WRAPPER, NOT A COPY. `d710` holds 570 lines of pipeline logic -- the TOF
switch that must reach both decode and estimate, the numeric bed sort, the
per-bed SINO lookup, the interpreter probing -- and a second copy would begin
to diverge at the first edit. This script therefore changes only the two things
apptainer changes, then runs the real `d710`:

  1. the image name becomes the .sif path (D710_IMAGE / D710_SIRF_IMAGE);
  2. apptainer_shim/ goes first on $PATH, so that every `docker` in the tree --
     d710's own, and equally vendor/run.sh's and utils/container.py's, which
     this script never touches -- is the shim and becomes `apptainer exec`.

WHAT WORKS, AND WHAT IT REQUIRES
  decode tostir read shell   apptainer and the d710 .sif; nothing else.
  estimate                   the same, plus --fakeroot, because GE's pet_recon
                             opens /usr/PET/systemConfig/cmcfg.xml read-write
                             and docker ran that step as root. `doctor` checks
                             it; apptainer_shim/docker prints the fallback if
                             it is missing.
  attn osem export           not here; use ./d710_isolate_stir_apptainer.sh
  lm lowdose                 no container either way: conda activate
                             petct_recon. This is where a GPU pays off.

THE GPU. The shim adds --nv whenever /dev/nvidiactl exists, so CUDA is visible
inside both images, but nothing inside them uses it today: sirf-local's STIR
links a CPU build of libparallelproj, and pet_recon's GPU path is forced off in
vendor/boot.gdb, GE never having shipped the .cl kernels. The one place a GPU
changes the figures in `./d710 --help` is `d710 lm`, which runs on the host
through PyTomography; install a CUDA torch in petct_recon and the TOF timings
in that table cease to matter.

BUILDING THE .sif FILES, on the machine holding the docker images:
  apptainer build d710_full.sif  docker-daemon://d710:full
  apptainer build sirf_local.sif docker-daemon://sirf-local:0.1
Then declare them once in D710/.env:
  D710_SIF=/path/to/d710_full.sif
  D710_SIRF_SIF=/path/to/sirf_local.sif
Without those lines they are looked for in $D710_SIF_DIR, D710/sif/, D710/,
$D710_OUT/sif and ~/sif.

ADDITIONAL ENVIRONMENT, beyond everything ./d710 --help lists:
  D710_SIF D710_SIRF_SIF   the two images
  D710_SIF_DIR             where to look for them
  D710_APPTAINER_BIN       the apptainer binary, if not on $PATH
  D710_APPTAINER_FAKEROOT  1 / 0 / auto           (see apptainer_shim/docker)
  D710_APPTAINER_OVERLAY   tmpfs / none / <dir>   the writable layer
  D710_APPTAINER_NV        1 / 0 / auto
  D710_APPTAINER_BIND      additional binds, space-separated
  D710_APPTAINER_QUIET     1 to stop echoing every apptainer command
USAGE
        echo
        echo "================ ./d710 --help ================"
        exec "$HERE/d710" --help
        ;;
    decode|estimate|tostir|exam|read|shell)
        _apt_need "d710:full" "${D710_SIF:-}" D710_SIF ;;
    attn|osem|export)
        if [[ -n "${D710_SIRF_SIF:-}" ]]; then
            echo ">> note: '$CMD' here needs SIRF installed on the HOST." >&2
            echo ">>       to run it in $D710_SIRF_SIF instead:" >&2
            echo ">>       ./d710_isolate_stir_apptainer.sh $*" >&2
        fi
        ;;
esac

exec "$HERE/d710" "$@"
